# Feature: GovOps Control Plane

Full spec: `doc/spec/govops-control-plane.md`

Companion: `doc/spec/civic-data-platform.md` (warehouse + SQL). This control plane **exports** `usage_daily` aggregates and **gates** `data:publish` via entitlements. It never exposes Paperclip OLTP to ad-hoc SQL.

## What it is

Ciutatis enrolls governments. Each government operates Paperclip: institutions (`companies`), channels (`agents`), requests (`issues`), objectives (`goals`), approvals, heartbeats, budgets. Platform staff set entitlements and meter usage. Government staff operate only their government.

## Identity lock

- `governments.id` **is** `government_id` (billing, RBAC, entitlements, usage).
- `tenant_instances` is the Cloudflare deploy/routing unit. `governments.tenant_instance_id` unique when hosted, null on self-host.
- Do not treat `tenant_instances.id` as `government_id`.

## RBAC lock

- Roles: government/institution `owner | admin | operator | viewer | auditor`. Platform: `platform_owner | platform_operator | platform_support | platform_auditor`.
- `grantsForHumanRole()` in `server/src/services/company-member-roles.ts` must **not** return `[]`.
- `assertCompanyAccess` is too coarse; mutating routes need `assertCompanyPermission` plus entitlement checks.
- Matrices live in the spec §5.

## Invariants (required behavior)

Single assignee, **atomic checkout** (code currently fails: Express `requestService.checkout` is an unconditional UPDATE and the route skips `assertCompanyAccess`), approval gates, heartbeat invoke/status/cancel, budget hard-stop, activity log on mutations.

Workers budget overview currently returns empty arrays — silent subset. Hosted must evaluate policies or fail closed.

## UI

One Next.js app: `apps/landing`. Government board under `/admin/:prefix/...`. Platform under `/admin/instance/settings/*`. Compact the board (drop `MyIssues`, orphan `IssueDetail`, UX labs). Shared host appendix: spec Appendix A.

## Dual runtime

Hosted civic SaaS = Workers + D1. Self-host = Express + Postgres. Contract in `packages/shared`. Unimplemented paths: **501** `{ error, availability }`, never `200 []`.

## Do not in this docs-only pass

Do not delete apps, implement RBAC enforcement, or add the `governments` table until a follow-up implementation PR.
